  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electric Boat has $10.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, distributed across 281 awards with an average award size of $38.5M. Electric Boat's obligations are down 49.4% year over year. Fiscal-year trends show peaks and troughs: obligations were $8.7B in FY21, $9.4B in FY22, $10.8B in FY23, $8.6B in FY24, $21.4B in FY25, and $10.8B in FY26. Electric Boat's work in FY2026 to date concentrates in Engineering Services at $6.9B and Ship Building and Repairing at $3.9B, with smaller amounts in specialized manufacturing and R&D categories. Electric Boat recorded single-market figures as small as $267K in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing and as much as $6.9B in Engineering Services. The mix of large program dollars and many awards implies continued reliance on a few high-dollar markets alongside a long tail of niche manufacturing and technical services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove the year-over-year change?",
        "body": "Electric Boat's obligations are down 49.4% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a large swing into FY25 with $21.4B, followed by a return to $10.8B in FY26. The FY26 total matches the FY23 total of $10.8B, indicating a reversion from the FY25 peak. Large program timing appears to be the primary driver of these swings."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are Electric Boat's FY2026 dollars concentrated?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market at $6.9B. Ship Building and Repairing is the next largest market at $3.9B. Several smaller markets together account for the remainder, including Instrument manufacturing at $2.4M and R&D at $1.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
